  "description": "Types shared by the GeometryHelper.PlaneGeometry and GeometryHelper.SolidGeometry libraries: a Tolerance carrying the thresholds every geometric comparison is measured against, an Angle that names its own unit, and the enumerations describing where a point sits relative to a shape or a plane. Referenced by both libraries so that a program using them together sees one Tolerance and one Angle rather than two of each.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
  "id": "GeometryHelper.CommonGeometry",
